name: "air_vm"
type: "system"
about: "
AiR VM — the executable entry point for the AiR language runtime.

Loads a .air program file, interprets it with the tree-walking interpreter,
and dispatches on the top-level 'type' binding:

  python_source   run the .py file named by 'name' (relative to the .air
                  file) with remaining CLI args forwarded as sys.argv.

Usage:
  ./air_vm <program.air> [args...]

Example:
  ./air_vm looking_glass/looking_glass.air ../looking_glass/

Future work: bytecode compilation, hotpath JIT, additional dispatch types.
"
